From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(network): discard packets after session disconnect

Discard inbound application packets once the application closes its session. Emit one packet per batch decode call so a Disconnect handled synchronously can stop the remaining packets in that batch.

ViaVersion stops translating after a session closes. Queued packets must not reach the Java decoder untranslated. Preserve this session boundary for NetherNet without depending on legacy transport events or codecs.

Embedded transport tests cover local close completion, queued packets during an asynchronous close, and a Disconnect followed by more packets in one batch.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/netty/BatchLengthCodec.java b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/netty/BatchLengthCodec.java
index ae2aa73ae77264a096a7873b7d4f23de791627d8..bb26952e74ae35a6b92f2af237bc0a25aba77093 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/netty/BatchLengthCodec.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/netty/BatchLengthCodec.java
@@ -36,14 +36,18 @@ public class BatchLengthCodec extends ByteToMessageCodec<ByteBuf> {
 
     @Override
     protected void decode(final ChannelHandlerContext ctx, final ByteBuf in, final List<Object> out) {
-        while (in.isReadable()) {
-            final int length = BedrockTypes.UNSIGNED_VAR_INT.readPrimitive(in);
-            if (in.isReadable(length)) {
-                out.add(in.readRetainedSlice(length));
-            } else { // Bedrock client drops the packet if the length is invalid
-                ViaBedrock.getPlatform().getLogger().log(Level.WARNING, "Dropping packet with invalid length: " + length + " (readable bytes: " + in.readableBytes() + ")");
-                in.skipBytes(in.readableBytes());
-            }
+        // Emit one packet per call so each is handled before the next is split. A packet such as Disconnect
+        // can close the session, and the rest of its batch must not reach the application afterwards.
+        if (DisconnectHandler.isClosed(ctx)) {
+            in.skipBytes(in.readableBytes());
+            return;
+        }
+        final int length = BedrockTypes.UNSIGNED_VAR_INT.readPrimitive(in);
+        if (in.isReadable(length)) {
+            out.add(in.readRetainedSlice(length));
+        } else { // Bedrock client drops the packet if the length is invalid
+            ViaBedrock.getPlatform().getLogger().log(Level.WARNING, "Dropping packet with invalid length: " + length + " (readable bytes: " + in.readableBytes() + ")");
+            in.skipBytes(in.readableBytes());
         }
     }
 
